# 2. PRIMARY REQUIREMENT: EVERY PUBLISHED COMPETENCY MUST HAVE A COURSE

The existing application contains approximately 99 published competencies, but only four flagship courses have been developed.

This leaves the majority of the competency catalogue without learning content.

The objective is to establish complete course coverage.

Existing flagship courses:

1. Frontend Development Foundations.
2. Graphic Design Foundations.
3. Digital Marketing Foundations.
4. Communication and Public Speaking.

Target:

- 99 published competencies.
- 99 properly associated foundational courses, assuming each competency is intended to have its own course.
- Four existing courses preserved and improved where necessary.
- Approximately 95 additional courses, subject to verification of existing associations and duplicates.

Do not duplicate existing courses.

Do not create a course for a competency that already has an appropriate published course.

Do not leave published competencies without a learning pathway unless there is an explicitly documented reason.

Every course must belong to its correct competency and category.

A competency must not receive an unrelated generic course simply to satisfy a numerical target.

