# 5. DEVELOP COURSE CONTENT THAT IS SPECIFIC TO EACH COMPETENCY

This requirement is critical.

Courses must be designed around their actual competencies.

For example:

### Communication & Interpersonal

Public Speaking must teach speech preparation, audience analysis, presentation structure, voice control, body language and delivery.

Negotiation Skills must teach preparation, interests, bargaining strategies, trade-offs, objections and agreement building.

Active Listening must teach listening techniques, clarification, questioning, interpretation and feedback.

Conflict Resolution must teach conflict identification, de-escalation, mediation, negotiation and resolution planning.

These courses must not share identical curricula simply because they belong to the same category.

### Writing & Content Creation

General Writing should address clarity, structure, grammar, editing and effective written communication.

Professional Writing should address workplace communication, formal documents, professional tone and business correspondence.

Technical Writing should address documentation, technical explanations, user instructions and information architecture.

Copywriting should address persuasive writing, audience research, headlines, calls to action and conversion-focused content.

### Entrepreneurship & Business

Business Planning should cover business models, market research, value propositions, operations and financial projections.

Sales should cover prospecting, customer discovery, presentations, objection handling and closing.

Financial Literacy should cover budgeting, saving, cash flow, financial planning and basic financial decisions.

### Digital Marketing & Social Media

SEO should cover keyword research, on-page optimisation, technical fundamentals and performance analysis.

Social Media Marketing should cover platform selection, content planning, audience engagement and analytics.

Content Marketing should cover audience needs, content strategy, production, distribution and measurement.

### Creative & Design

Graphic Design should cover design principles, typography, colour, layout and production.

UI/UX Design should cover user research, information architecture, wireframing, prototyping and usability testing.

Photography should cover exposure, composition, lighting, framing and editing.

### Technology & Digital

Frontend Development should cover HTML, CSS, JavaScript, responsive design, DOM manipulation and deployment.

Data Analysis should cover data collection, cleaning, analysis, visualisation and interpretation.

Cybersecurity Fundamentals should cover security principles, threats, safe practices, access control and risk awareness.

### Career & Professional Development

CV Writing should cover structure, achievement statements, tailoring and professional presentation.

Interview Readiness should cover preparation, question handling, communication and interview practice.

Project Management should cover planning, scope, scheduling, execution, risk and evaluation.

These are examples of the required level of specificity, not an exhaustive list. Generate the complete curricula using the actual competency records in Supabase.

