# 10. COURSE COMPLETION RULES

Do not mark a course complete merely because all lessons have been opened.

Use the existing course completion architecture and extend it where necessary.

Course completion should support configurable requirements, including:

- Required lessons completed.
- Required activities completed.
- Required quizzes passed.
- Required practical assignments submitted.
- Required practical challenges approved.

Distinguish between:

- Not started.
- In progress.
- Awaiting assessment.
- Needs improvement.
- Completed.
- Completed with practical evidence approved.

A learner must not receive a verified practical competency status simply for uploading a file.

Only authorized assessment workflows may approve practical evidence.

